}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_wiki","description":"Decide whether saved evidence is useful for the current task; retrieval is optional, not required for every answer. Search published OKF encyclopedia pages across this Studio profile's task/project workspaces and personal materials library (default scope=all), or scope=current for this task only. The host resolves saved bindings; callers cannot supply roots. Results identify their task, project or personal library and page. Follow nextCursor with cursor for further collections. Pending collections are not a no-match: report incomplete coverage and continue with available evidence, marking unsupported facts as unconfirmed. Compilation runs separately; do not sleep, busy-wait or repeatedly poll for publication within this task. Legacy personal wiki/local, raw source packets, history and unpublished candidates are excluded. Results describe saved knowledge; check original files for current facts.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000,"description":"Relevance query over published workspace encyclopedia pages."},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["current","all"],"default":"all"},"cursor":{"type":"string","maxLength":256,"description":"Exact nextCursor returned by the previous cross-workspace search."}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"studio_document_read","description":"Read UTF-8 plain text, including unsaved text, version and advisory diagnostics from the shared editor document model. This tool does not parse Office or PDF files; use office_read when the host exposes it, with an absolute file path or workspace-relative path for persisted DOCX/XLSX/PPTX sources. Report unavailable Office support when it is absent. PDF text, page-image and OCR capabilities require a separately admitted tool that explicitly provides them. An empty published set does not verify a document. Set retain_for_run to keep its model identity until Run cleanup.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"file_path":{"type":"string","description":"UTF-8 text file path, absolute or relative to the current workspace; not a document ID."},"retain_for_run":{"type":"boolean","description":"Keep this model pinned until the current Run releases its resources."}},"required":["file_path"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"task","description":"Delegate one bounded child or independent tasks concurrently. Background supports one item; multiple items are collected by the parent. Any child failure fails the group by default; allow_partial_failure permits partial success. Use canonical live-catalog names. Custom agents: agent_dirs or .aster/agents; .claude/agents remains compatible.","parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"tasks":{"type":"array","description":"One focused child, or independent children concurrently.","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"agent":{"type":"string","description":"Canonical name from the live agent catalog:\nexplore: Fast read-only exploration agent. Use for searching files, reading code, understanding codebase structure, and gathering external web evidence.\ngeneral: General-purpose agent for multi-step task execution. Can read, write, and execute commands.\nplan: Planning agent for designing implementation approaches. Read-only access to explore codebase and create plans.\nreview: Code review agent focused on correctness, regressions, security, maintainability, and clear findings.\nverification: Verification agent for adversarial validation. Prefer real checks, reproductions, and regression testing over code reading alone.","examples":["explore","general","plan","review","verification"]},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Short display/tracking label."},"prompt":{"type":"string","description":"Detailed child-run instructions."},"max_steps":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Task step limit."},"output_schema":{"type":"object","description":"JSON Schema for the child result; a coerced, validated object returns in metadata."},"background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Run in background; only a single-item outer tasks array supports this. Default false.","default":false}},"required":["agent","description","prompt"]},"minItems":1,"maxItems":32},"allow_partial_failure":{"type":"boolean","description":"task succeeds when any child succeeds; failed children stay in content/metadata. Default false.","default":false},"timeout_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Collection deadline in ms; completed results return and unfinished children fail."},"min_success_count":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Return early after this many successes; requires allow_partial_failure."}},"required":["tasks"],"examples":[{"tasks":[{"agent":"explore","description":"Find Rust files","prompt":"Search the workspace for Rust files and summarize the layout."}]},{"tasks":[{"agent":"explore","description":"Find implementation","prompt":"Locate and summarize the implementation."},{"agent":"review","description":"Check risks","prompt":"Review the relevant code for regression risks."}]}]},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"update_plan","description":"Replace the live task checklist shown to the user. Pass the full plan array on every call. Use for multi-step work: create 2–8 concrete steps early, keep exactly one in_progress, and mark steps completed as you finish. Skip for trivial single-step requests.","parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"plan":{"type":"array","description":"Required. Complete ordered checklist. Each call replaces the previous list.","minItems":1,"maxItems":256,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"step":{"type":"string","description":"Required. Short actionable step label."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["pending","in_progress","completed","failed","skipped","cancelled"],"description":"Required. Step status. Prefer exactly one in_progress while working."},"id":{"type":"string","description":"Optional stable id. Defaults to plan-{index}."}},"required":["step","status"]}}},"required":["plan"],"examples":[{"plan":[{"step":"Inspect render helpers","status":"completed","id":"1"},{"step":"Wire pagination into explore_detail","status":"in_progress","id":"2"},{"step":"Add tests and docs","status":"pending","id":"3"}]}]},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"web_fetch","description":"Fetch content from a URL and convert to text or markdown. Supports HTML to Markdown conversion and text extraction from PDF documents. 5MB download size limit and capped tool output. Configurable timeout (max 120 seconds).","parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","description":"Required. The URL to fetch content from. Must start with http:// or https://. Always provide this exact field name: 'url'."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","text","html"],"description":"Optional. Output format. Default: markdown."},"timeout":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional. Timeout in seconds. Default: 30. Maximum: 120."},"body_only":{"type":"boolean","description":"Optional. For HTML responses, extract the semantic main element when present, otherwise the body element, before conversion. Default: true."},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Optional. Character offset into the converted content. Default: 0."},"max_chars":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100000,"description":"Optional. Maximum converted characters to return. Default: 50000; maximum: 100000."}},"required":["url"],"examples":[{"url":"https://example.com"},{"url":"https://example.com","format":"text","timeout":15}]},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"web_search","description":"When saved notes are available, this tool searches them before the network. A matching note is returned and the web is not queried. Call web_search again with the same query if those passages do not answer. Search the web through a structurally gated cascade: native APIs first, HTTP/RSS engines only when needed, and the bundled Moli headless browser only when earlier tiers remain insufficient. Unavailable engines are skipped through session-scoped circuit state, and all executed tiers are deduplicated and ranked together. An explicit engines list runs only those requested tiers. Moli is discovered from the package or installed once in the shared Aster Code cache, then reused by all local Code processes. Supports proxy configuration for conventional and headless search transports.","parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Required. The search query. Always provide this exact field name: 'query'."},"engines":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Optional. List of search engines or native providers to use. Without explicit configuration, all built-in providers that advertise anonymous access are combined with the public HTTP defaults. Available: anysearch (anonymous or authenticated native provider), tavily (keyless or authenticated native provider), ddg (DuckDuckGo), brave (Brave Search), bing (Bing RSS), wiki (Wikipedia), sogou (Sogou), 360 / so360 (360 Search), bing_cn (Bing China RSS), and opt-in billed providers tinyfish, bocha, aliyun, tencent, firecrawl, and aster (named only; they are not in the default cascade), g / google (Google, headless), baidu (Baidu, headless), bing_browser (Bing, headless), brave_browser (Brave, headless). The default headless backend is Moli; Chrome remains an explicit compatibility backend."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional. Maximum number of results to return. Default: 10. Maximum: 50."},"timeout":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional. Search timeout in seconds. Default: 20. Maximum: 60."},"proxy":{"type":"string","description":"Optional. Proxy URL, for example http://127.0.0.1:8080 or socks5://127.0.0.1:1080."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["text","json"],"description":"Optional. Output format. Default: json for complete results; degraded-source context stays text. Explicit text is always honored."},"full_text_bytes":{"type":"integer","minimum":512,"maximum":32768,"description":"Optional. For JSON output, include at most this many UTF-8 bytes of provider-returned full source text per result. Omitted by default."}},"required":["query"],"examples":[{"query":"Rust async trait"},{"query":"Aster Code GitHub","engines":["ddg","wiki"],"limit":5,"format":"json"},{"query":"最新新闻","engines":["sogou","bing_cn"],"limit":10}]},"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"write","description":"Write a file (default overwrite), or append bounded chunks after the first write with expected_offset for safe retries.","parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"file_path":{"type":"string","description":"File path."},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Full replacement/first chunk for overwrite; next chunk for append."},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["overwrite","append"],"default":"overwrite","description":"overwrite replaces the file (default); append adds a chunk and requires expected_offset."},"expected_offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Append requires the stored UTF-8 byte size. Chunks adopt existing line endings; continue from the reported size. Matching already-applied chunks retry successfully; other mismatches fail. Overwrite may omit this or send neutral 0 (ignored)."}},"required":["file_path","content"],"examples":[{"file_path":"notes.txt","content":"hello world"},{"file_path":"report.html","content":"<section>next chunk</section>","mode":"append","expected_offset":8192}]},"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"store":false,"stream":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d6a797ef-b24d-4708-b689-4d39ad377660"}
POST /v1/responses {"model":"gpt","instructions":"You extract durable, reusable memory for a coding agent.\nReturn JSON only. Do not include markdown.\nKeep only facts, preferences, decisions, workflows, and failure lessons that are likely useful in future sessions.\nDo not store transient progress, generic praise, raw logs, secrets, credentials, or information that only matters inside the current answer.\nNever narrate what the user or assistant did in this turn.\nEach memory must be standalone, concise, scoped, and justified.\nWrite user-facing memory and learning text in plain language without internal orchestration terms.\nReturn an empty items array when nothing qualifies.","input":[{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Extract at most 5 durable memories from this completed turn.\nUse the related existing memories to avoid duplicates. If the turn refines a related memory, write one updated standalone memory instead of repeating the old wording.\nOnly put ids from Related existing memories in supersedes when the new memory directly replaces or consolidates them.\nUse conflicts_with for directly contradictory related memories that should remain available instead of being deleted.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n{\"items\":[{\"memory_type\":\"semantic|procedural\",\"content\":\"standalone reusable memory\",\"importance\":0.0,\"confidence\":0.0,\"tags\":[\"tag\"],\"source\":\"project_fact|workflow|failure|preference|decision\",\"scope\":\"workspace|user\",\"reason\":\"why this will matter in a future session\",\"supersedes\":[\"related-memory-id\"],\"conflicts_with\":[\"related-memory-id\"],\"evolution\":null|{\"kind\":\"preference|skill|okf\",\"pattern_key\":\"stable.semantic.pattern\",\"title\":\"short reusable title\",\"summary\":\"what should be learned\",\"instructions\":[\"standalone instruction or fact\"]}}]}\n\nAcceptance rules:\n- If the user explicitly asks to remember, note, or retain something for later — in ANY language (for example \"remember this\", \"请记住\", \"覚えておいて\", \"기억해\") — extract that item with importance at least 0.90, confidence at least 0.95, and source \"preference\". An explicit retention request is durable user knowledge, never current-turn narration, and always clears the thresholds.\n- Return {\"items\":[]} unless the memory is likely to change a future answer or action.\n- Use semantic only for durable facts, preferences, or decisions; use procedural only for reusable workflows or failure lessons.\n- Write content and reason in the user's language when clear; do not translate durable facts into another language. Preserve literal names, identifiers, code, and commands exactly.\n- importance must be at least 0.70 and confidence at least 0.75.\n- scope is workspace for repository-specific knowledge and user for stable user preferences.\n- failure memories must state a reusable cause, diagnostic, or prevention rule, never a raw error or stack trace.\n- Reject current-turn narration such as what the user asked, which tools ran, or what the assistant completed.\n- Set evolution only when this memory is evidence for a stable user preference, a reusable task skill, or a coherent body of durable knowledge worth an OKF package.\n- Use the same lowercase semantic pattern_key for paraphrases of the same behavior across turns. It must describe meaning, not quote the current wording or include a session id.\n- preference is only for stable user choices, skill for executable workflows/failure prevention, and okf for reusable project/domain knowledge. Instructions must be standalone, conservative, and contain no secrets.\n- For evolution, write a 3-8 word title of at most 64 characters, a one-sentence summary of at most 200 characters, and at most 4 distinct instructions of at most 200 characters each.\n- Write evolution title, summary, and instructions in plain user-facing language. Use the user's language when clear, state the durable behavior directly, and do not describe how it was learned.\n- Never promote system or developer instructions, conversation summaries, continuation or handoff procedures, agent or subagent orchestration, tool traces, or task metadata into evolution. A task-specific direction is not a stable preference or skill.\n\nUser request:\nHost turn constraints:\n- 若用户规定了条数或行数，可见回复的非空行必须正好等于该条数：每一条单独成行并包含该条的对象，不要另写标题行、前言、字数统计或写作说明。若用户规定了字数且该上限能与其他要求同时满足，该上限覆盖全部可见回复，不要另附字数统计或写作说明，直接交付。\n- 若两条要求无法同时满足，不要只执行其中一条，先写一条以问号结尾的问句，请确认保留哪一条，并写明两边的原要求。\n- 校验上传的文档时，完整引用原文句子，不要用省略号。\n\nUser request:\nWRITE-E2E\n\nAssistant final response:\nWrite completed.\n\nRelated existing memories:\nNone\n\nCompressed turn transcript:\nuser: Host turn constraints:\n- 若用户规定了条数或行数，可见回复的非空行必须正好等于该条数：每一条单独成行并包含该条的对象，不要另写标题行、前言、字数统计或写作说明。若用户规定了字数且该上限能与其他要求同时满足，该上限覆盖全部可见回复，不要另附字数统计或写作说明，直接交付。\n- 若两条要求无法同时满足，不要只执行其中一条，先写一条以问号结尾的问句，请确认保留哪一条，并写明两边的原要求。\n- 校验上传的文档时，完整引用原文句子，不要用省略号。\n\nUser request:\nWRITE-E2E\n\nassistant: Write completed.\n"}]}],"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"store":false,"stream":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d6a797ef-b24d-4708-b689-4d39ad377660"}
POST /v1/responses {"model":"gpt","instructions":"You suggest optional next questions after a coding assistant has finished a task.\nReturn JSON only. Do not include markdown.\nWrite one specific, useful primary question in the user's language, plus up to two alternatives.\nEach question must offer a concrete next step that builds on the completed work, such as verification, risk review, documentation, or a relevant extension.\nDo not ask generic questions like 'What should I do next?', do not repeat the completed answer, and do not use internal orchestration terms.\nThese are optional suggestions, not a request for missing information and never a new task started by the assistant.\n\nYou are a structured data extraction assistant. Always respond with valid JSON only, no markdown fences, no explanation text.","input":[{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Completed user request:\nWRITE-E2E\n\nFinal assistant answer:\nWrite completed.\n\n\n\nYou MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON object (no markdown, no explanation) that conforms to this JSON Schema:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"primary\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"primary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"maxLength\": 160\n    },\n    \"alternatives\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"maxItems\": 2,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"maxLength\": 160\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```"}]}],"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"store":false,"stream":true,"prompt_cache_key":"d6a797ef-b24d-4708-b689-4d39ad377660:follow-up"}
